constraint_tests_clprtest	^test3\(\[	CEO-1934, the cfo 2026-11-26: the order of the list dump/3 returns is the order of the clpr store, an accident of the library's version (XSB 5.0.0's clpqr prints [x > 3.0,y > 4.0], swipl's 9.0.4, which SCRIP vendors, prints [y > 4.0,x > 3.0] on swipl itself); the program prints the list unsorted, so its order is no answer
constraint_tests_clprtest	^test22\(\[	CEO-1934, the cfo 2026-11-26: XSB 5.0.0's clpqr wraps a nonlinear residual of dump/3 in braces and swipl's 9.0.4 (SCRIP's, the same on swipl itself) does not; the same constraint, printed by two versions of one library, is no answer
constraint_tests_clprtest	^test27\(2\.71828182	CEO-1934, the cfo 2026-11-26: e(8,E) stops its series at a bound of 1.0e-10, and both 2.71828182845373 (XSB) and 2.71828182853849 (SCRIP and swipl) are within it; the digits past the bound are the library's float epsilon, no answer
constraint_tests_clprtest	^test30\(z\s*=	CEO-1934, the cfo 2026-11-26: XSB 5.0.0's clpqr leaves float noise -1.13686837721616e-13 in the residual of inf/4, swipl leaves 30.000000000000007*x, SCRIP 30.0*x; the noise of a float simplex is no answer
constraint_tests_clprtest	^test31\(z\s*=	CEO-1934, the cfo 2026-11-26: the same float noise as test30 in the residual of sup/4's twin, no answer
